title: Outside_Of_Office
---
<<play_music SoundManager act_2>> 
Ashe finds herself standing outside the Winslow building before she’s even fully considered what she’s doing. 
The towering glass façade reflects the grey sky above.
Its polished entrance is guarded by security personnel who look as though they’ve never had to worry about where they’ll sleep at night. 
She stares up at the highest floors, anger simmering beneath her skin. Somewhere inside this building are the answers she needs, and she’s determined to find them.
===


title: Enter_Office
---
<<declare $entered_office = false>>
<<if $entered_office == false>>
	Her phone vibrates.
	<<play_sfx SoundManager phone_ring>> 
	Teddy is calling her.
	<<show_evidence GameManager "Teddy Call">>
	She hesitates before answering, already bracing herself for the lecture.
	<<hide_evidence GameManager>>
	<<stop_sfx SoundManager>>
	<<start_character_conv CharacterManager "Ashe" "Teddy">>
	<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Teddy" "angry">>
	Teddy: Where the hell are you, Ashe?
	She winces at the familiar, clipped tone. Even retired, Teddy still sounds like a police officer questioning a suspect.
	Ashe: Out.
	Teddy: Out where?
	Ashe: Why does it matter?
	Teddy: Because you stormed out of the house, and I know you well enough to know you’re probably doing something stupid.
	<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Ashe" "shout">>
	Ashe: I’m not doing anything stupid! ... I’m just trying to fix something for once.
	There’s a pause.
	<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Teddy" "sad">>
	Teddy: Ashe, please. Just come home.
	<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Ashe" "default">>
	For a moment, guilt threatens to get the better of her. Teddy has enough to worry about without her adding to it, but she can’t bear the thought of returning home empty-handed.
	Ashe: I’ll be fine. I promise.
	She ends the call before he can argue.
	<<end_character_conv CharacterManager>>
	<<start_character_conv CharacterManager "Ashe">>
	Ashe: ... 
	<<end_character_conv CharacterManager>>
	<<set $entered_office = true>>
<<else>>
	<<declare $try_pick_lock = false>>
	<<if $try_pick_lock == false>>
		Approaching the building, Ashe keeps her head down, slipping past a guard who lurks outside and towards a quieter area around the back of the building.
		<<set $try_pick_lock = true>>
	<<endif>>
	She checks the door. It's closed, but she might be able to pick the lock.
	-> Try to pick the lock
		<<play_minigame MinigameManager "Lockpick" "Lockpick_Success" "Lockpick_Fail">>
	-> Find another way inside
		Ashe: ... Not a good idea.
<<endif>>
===


title: Locked_Door
---
... The door is locked.
===


title: Lockpick_Success
---
... Got it.  
<<goto_room GameManager "Stairwell">>
<<wait 2>>
The door unlocked, Ashe opens it to climb through as quietly as she can.
The stairwell is dim and smells faintly of concrete and cleaning products. 
She glances upwards. The stairs stretch several floors above her, disappearing around a series of landings. 
It's going to take longer than the lift, but at least she won't have to risk being noticed on a camera or questioned by anyone sharing the ride.
She starts climbing.
She pauses on a landing on the first floor, listening carefully for footsteps on the other side of the door. Nothing. Just the low hum of the building's ventilation.
Ashe pushes on, keeping close to the wall and checking the floor numbers until she reaches the highest level.
<<goto_room GameManager "Second Floor">>
===

title: Lockpick_Fail
---
...Shit. Someone's coming. 
<<wait 2>>
...
Let me try that again. 
<<play_minigame MinigameManager "Lockpick" "Lockpick_Success" "Lockpick_Fail">>
===

title: Locked_Door_Check
---
<<if $security_guard_present == false>>
	<<declare $door_1_checked = false>>
	<<declare $doors_checked = 0>>
	...This door is locked. A keycard is required to unlock it
	<<jump Security_Guard_Entrance>>
<<endif>>

===

title: Security_Guard_Entrance
---
<<declare $security_guard_present = false>>
<<wait 1>>
Ashe: ... Shit. 
Ashe punches the door, frustrated. 
Hearing the sound of incoming footsteps, she hides behind a corner. 
Security Guard: Yawn. No one comes around here anyway. I don't know why I have to be stationed up here.
Security Guard: It's not like anyone has the security card except for me. 
<<start_character_conv CharacterManager "Ashe">>
Ashe: ... 
<<end_character_conv CharacterManager>>
<<enable_object GameManager Security>>
<<set $security_guard_present = true>>
===

title: Security_Guard
---
The security guard looks out of the window, distracted.
-> Try take his card
	Ashe: ... Here goes nothing.
	<<play_minigame MinigameManager "Steal" "Stole_Keys" "Steal_Fail">>
	<<disable_object GameManager Security>>
-> Decide against it
	Ashe: ... This is such a dumb idea.
===

title: Steal_Fail
---
Ashe: I think he noticed me! 
...
<<wait 2>>
Ashe: Let me try that again. 
<<play_minigame MinigameManager "Steal" "Stole_Keys" "Steal_Fail">>
===
title: Stole_Keys
---
<<show_evidence GameManager "Keycard">>
<<obtain_evidence GameManager "Keycard">>
You got the Security Keycard.
<<hide_evidence GameManager>>
Ashe: ... Gotta wait for him to leave. 
...
Ashe: This better work.
...
She slips inside.
<<goto_room GameManager "Victor Office">>
<<jump Inside_Victor_Office>>
===

title: Inside_Victor_Office
---
<<play_music SoundManager Victor_1>> 
<<wait 2>>
The office is immaculate, all dark wood and floor-to-ceiling windows. Victor is nowhere to be seen, exactly the opportunity Ashe needs.
===

title: Victor_PC_1
---
<<declare $seen_pc_1 = false>>
<<if $seen_pc_1 ==false >>
	<<if $seen_pc_2 == false>>
		<<show_evidence GameManager "Winslow Purchases">>
		What's this?
		He's been buying properties... but they're all empty. 
		<<hide_evidence GameManager>>

	<<else>>
		...
		Even more properties listed here. This is insane. 
	<<endif>>
	<<set $seen_pc_1 = true>>
<<else>>
	...
<<endif>>
===

