title: Teddy_Case
---
<<show_evidence GameManager "Teddy Case">>
Ashe finds her father's name.
A file detailing his accident sits among the paperwork, marked with confidential annotations.
You got Teddy's Accident Report.
Ashe: Someone blocked the inspector from questioning Victor… and the fact he even has this police report in his office…
<<obtain_evidence GameManager "Teddy Case">>
<<hide_evidence GameManager>>
<<jump Pursuer>>
===

title: Pursuer
---
<<play_sfx_one_shot SoundManager text>>
Before she can read further, her phone lights up.
Unknown: We know what you're doing. Walk away before you get hurt.
Ashe stares at the message, her pulse quickening.
Someone knows she's here.
And she’s already found enough evidence to make her stomach turn, but her father's accident report keeps drawing her attention back. 
The report mentions an internal investigation, missing pages she couldn't see at the flat, and a handwritten telephone number tucked into the back of the file, with the name scribbled out.
Ashe: ... I have to call them.
<<enable_object GameManager Call_Colleague>>
===

title: Call_Colleague
---
<<declare $phone_broken = false>>
<<if $phone_broken == false>> 
	Ashe pulls out her phone and dials, glancing towards the office door as she waits for someone to answer.
	<<play_sfx SoundManager phone_ring_anon>>
	ring...ring...
	<<stop_sfx SoundManager>>
	<<start_character_conv CharacterManager "Ashe">>
	Unknown: Hello?
	Ashe: My name’s Ashe. I found your number in a case file about Teddy’s accident. He’s my dad.
	The silence on the other end tightens her grip on the phone.
	Unknown: What have you found?
	Ashe: I’m in Victor Winslow’s office. I found documents connecting him to the evictions, and there’s a file about my dad’s accident. 
	Ashe: I think he was investigating Winslow before it happened. Do you know anything about that?
	A sharp breath crackles through the speaker.
	Unknown: Your father was looking into Winslow’s property dealings. Families were being forced out of their homes, and Teddy started connecting the evictions to some very questionable financial arrangements. 
	Unknown: Then the cases started disappearing. Witnesses withdrew their statements, and we were ordered to stop asking questions.
	Ashe’s eyes dart towards the office door.
	<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Ashe" "angry">>
	Ashe: Who ordered it? Was Winslow involved in my dad’s accident?
	Unknown: I can't prove he was responsible for the accident, but Teddy was getting close to something powerful people wanted buried. Listen, you need to get out of that building. If Winslow’s people discover-
	The call crackles violently.
	Ashe: Hello? Are you still there?
	<<end_character_conv CharacterManager>>
	<<show_evidence GameManager "Ashe Phone">>
	Her phone screen flickers, briefly displaying a jumble of coloured lines before going completely black.
	Ashe stares at it.
	She presses the power button. 
	Nothing. 
	It's not working.
	<<hide_evidence GameManager>>
	Ashe: What am I meant to do?
	A cold sensation creeps up her spine. The phone had been working perfectly moments ago. Now, just as she was about to learn something important, it had suddenly stopped.
	Then the telephone in Victor's office rings.
	<<set $phone_broken = true>>
	<<change_location GameManager "Winslow Building 2">>
<<else>>
	It's no use. It won't turn on.
<<endif>>
===

